    "recommendations": "Reducing direct vegetation contact with the structure and creating greater separation between shrubs, brush, and the building perimeter could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near improvements. Managing the tree cluster to increase vertical clearance and reduce horizontal fuel connectivity between ground-level vegetation and tree canopies may further support defensible space objectives. The continuous grass cover and scattered shrubs across the property contribute to a connected fuel mosaic that could benefit from periodic mowing or thinning to interrupt fuel continuity across open terrain. Maintaining cleared margins along the length of the driveway would support firefighter access and improve evacuation route reliability, particularly given the extended driveway length. Addressing brush concentrations immediately adjacent to the structure should be prioritized, as reducing direct fuel contact with the building perimeter may reduce structure exposure and support suppression operations during a wildfire event."
